            "review_title": "Review at Bun Cha Ca Ba Phien",
            "review_text": "BL_Leo\nPetaling Jaya, Malaysia4050 contributions\n0\nVery good seafood noodle\nApr 2020 • Family\nAn almost full day tour in the city of Da Nang under the hot weather could get everyone hungry easily. We had run out of ideas on what to eat - so when our tour guide picked us up from the designated point, I asked “what do you normally eat here? Something nice and cheap” \n\nLess than 10 minutes later, he stopped ya in front of this basic-looking restaurant where the people were seen enjoying their bowl of delicious looking bowl of noodle. I took a look at their menu and realised that they specialised in fish noodle... mainly tuna (more like mackarel tuna or ikan tongkol) and mackarel meat. \n\nPrice-wise it starts from 25,000VND to 85,000VND depending on what you order. The soup was brimming with the sweetness from the fish and also some grilled meat. On the seafood option, I found myself chomping down the tuna.. as I love Nasi dagang very much which uses the same fish. \n\nIt was lunch time so the crowd spilled outside the walkway, and since our driver was so helpful.. we decided to buy him lunch as well as a token of appreciation for bringing us to such a nice and affordable feast\nRead more\nWritten April 16, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-04",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
